ened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jul 22, 2013 it closed at $23.64, its first close above the base high of $23.14. Volume that day was 9.3M shares, 1.68x the prior 10-day average of 5.5M. It didn't hold. By Jul 26, 2013 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $22.00.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}